    <p class="profile-summary" id="summary"><em>Socrates (c. 470–399 BCE) was an Athenian philosopher who wrote nothing, so that his thought is known through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plato">Plato</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a> and others. He questioned Athenians about virtue and claimed ignorance, and in 399 BCE he was convicted of impiety and corrupting the youth and executed with hemlock.</em></p>

